A correct answer should compute the pad from the known pair and XOR it with the second ciphertext, while checking lengths.
```pseudocode
function recoverSecondPlaintext(knownPlaintext, knownCiphertext, secondCiphertext):
    if length(knownPlaintext) != length(knownCiphertext):
        raise Error("known plaintext and ciphertext lengths differ")
    if length(secondCiphertext) > length(knownPlaintext):
        raise Error("not enough recovered pad bytes")

    pad = new byte array of length(knownPlaintext)
    for i from 0 to $length(knownPlaintext) - 1$:
        pad[i] = knownPlaintext[i] XOR knownCiphertext[i]

    recovered = new byte array of length(secondCiphertext)
    for i from 0 to $length(secondCiphertext) - 1$:
        recovered[i] = secondCiphertext[i] XOR pad[i]

    return recovered
```
